data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_01bc828f75143ae0016a05775529188191a0227ad5ba07ff63","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":715,"text":"I can’t directly render the image here, but I can give you a production-ready prompt/spec to use with an image generator or artist.\n\n**Prompt:**\n\nCreate **exactly one** clean **HD 2D game asset** of an **Ace of Spades playing card**, using the input image as the visual reference for the **existing compact square-ish card silhouette, readable poker-card proportions, corner rank layout, and central suit clarity**.\n\n### Composition\n- Show **one single centered card only**\n- Card must be **fully visible** with **generous empty margin** around it\n- **No sheet grid**\n- **No extra cards**\n- **No background scene**\n- **No hands**\n- **No table**\n- **No UI**\n- Asset should read clearly at small scale for a **Godot 2D card game**\n\n### Background\n- Background must be **100% solid flat magenta: `#FF00FF`**\n- **No gradient**\n- **No texture**\n- **No shadows on background**\n- Card isolated cleanly for **chroma-key processing**\n\n### Card shape and layout\n- Preserve the reference card’s **compact poker-card silhouette**\n- Keep the **same readable rank placement**:\n  - large **“A”** in the **top-left corner**\n  - matching **upside-down “A”** in the **bottom-right corner**\n  - small spade icons near each corner rank\n- Keep a **large central spade symbol**\n- Maintain **simple gameplay readability**\n- Ensure rank and suit remain legible when scaled to **128x128**\n\n### Ocean theme styling\nRedesign the card face with a restrained underwater aesthetic:\n- **Pearly white card face**\n- **Thin coral-and-shell border**\n- **Subtle teal wave pattern**\n- **Small bubbles**\n- **Faint sea-glass highlights**\n- **Soft aqua shadows**\n- Use restrained colors only:\n  - pearl white\n  - seafoam teal\n  - deep navy\n  - small coral accents\n  - soft aqua shadows\n\n### Suit design\n- Central spade must be **deep navy**\n- Shape the spade like a **stylized manta ray** or **tidepool silhouette**\n- It must **still clearly read as a spade at a glance**\n- Corner spade symbols should match the central suit style in a simplified readable form\n\n### Style\n- **Clean HD 2D game asset**\n- **Crisp edges**\n- **Minimal, elegant decorative detail**\n- **Readable, production-friendly**\n- Slight stylization is fine, but avoid clutter\n- No extra text beyond:\n  - **“A”**\n  - spade symbols\n\n### Output requirements\n- **Exactly one centered card asset**\n- **Full card visible**\n- **Solid magenta background only**\n- **No other objects**\n\n**Suggested negative prompt:**\nmultiple cards, card sheet, deck, hand holding card, casino table, background scene, UI, text labels, numbers other than A, hearts, clubs, diamonds, ornate frame, excessive detail, muddy colors, photorealism, 3D render, angled perspective, cropped card, drop shadows on magenta background, gradient magenta background\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into:\n1. a **short SDXL prompt**,  \n2. a **pixel-art adapted prompt**, or  \n3. a **Godot-ready asset spec with exact image dimensions**."}

